    rdfs:label "Little Bill Daggett" ;
    schema1:description "Authoritarian Self-Righteousness: Enforcing a personal version of justice through a rigid interpretation of the law to validate the use of excessive and systemic violence. | Sadistic Dominance: Deriving psychological satisfaction from physically brutalizing others to maintain an unchallenged position of absolute power within a social hierarchy. | Moral Hypocrisy: Condemning the violent nature of outlaws and gunslingers while simultaneously employing ruthless tactics and disregarding the inherent dignity of victims. | Cynical Pragmatism: Rejecting idealized notions of heroism or fairness in favor of a cold belief that only those with the unyielding will to exert violence can maintain order. | Symbolic Incompetence: Manifesting internal moral flaws and a lack of true structural integrity through the obsessive yet failed construction of a personal domain, exemplified by a leaking house." ;
